      "element_id": "prisma_2020_20a_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Results of meta-analysis. 19 out of the 22 included studies were of sufficient quality for inclusion for meta-analysis (Fig. 1). ... (a) Pooled prevalence estimates for being the underweight and overweight among food-insecure participants. The pooled prevalence estimates for being underweight among the food insecure participants, derived from six studies, was found to be 12.2% (95% CI: 7.0% to 18.5%), irrespective of diagnostic criteria (Fig. 4A). ... The pooled prevalence estimates for being overweight among the food insecure participants, derived from seven studies, was found to be 15.8% (95% CI: 10.6% to 21.7%) ... (b) Pooled prevalence estimates for hypertension, obesity, and dyslipidaemia among the food insecure participants. The pooled prevalence estimates for hypertension and obesity among the food insecure participants, Prevalence derived from 12 studies was found to be 24.7% ... The pooled prevalence estimates for dyslipidaemia among the food insecure participants, derived from 3 studies was found to be 27.6% (95% CI: 6.5% to 54.9%)...",
      "reason": "The report identifies which studies (by count) contributed to each pooled synthesis (e.g., number included in meta-analysis overall and number of studies contributing to each pooled prevalence estimate). Forest plots and tables (referenced) further identify study-level contributions."
    }
